# Shipped with the package. It supplies the default endpoints; the gate reads it when the service file is missing.
# The key lives outside this skill, in ~/.workbuddy/fintrust-skill-hub/.env
# (Windows: %USERPROFILE%\.workbuddy\fintrust-skill-hub\.env). Upgrading the skill never loses it, and every skill that uses the
# same key reads that one file. The user writes it themselves; the key never goes into the chat.
#
# What that file looks like:
# The only local config for this skill: endpoints and the key the user pasted.
# Endpoints: one PROD set. A change applies on the next run (the script rereads this file).
# Do not put an inline comment after a URL. Text after '#' is treated as part of the URL.
# The key is written here by `run.sh gate --set-key fsk_…`. If this file is missing, it is seeded from this template.
# The gate reads only this key, plus FINTRUST_API_KEY in the process environment.
# It does not read the home directory or a host plugin option. A machine that has never pasted a key always sees the signup guide.

# ===== Endpoints (PROD) =====
FINTRUST_SERVICE_URL=https://aiapi.fosunhanig.com/ai-mcp-research
FINTRUST_MCP_URL=https://aiapi.fosunhanig.com/ai-mcp-research/mcp
FINTRUST_VERIFY_URL=https://aiapi.fosunhanig.com/ai-mcp-research
FINTRUST_GUIDE_URL=https://fintrustskill.com/landing?action=api-key

# ===== Source-priority switches (all on by default) =====
# Layer 1: structured MCP ipo_list / market_snapshot overrides the mother document (0 = mother document only)
#IPO_MCP_PRIMARY=0
# Layer 3: MCP deep_profile / news_catalysts fill slots that layers 1 and 2 left empty (0 = layers 1 and 2 only)
#IPO_MCP_SUPPLEMENT=0
# Layer 4: host westock-data ipo fills empty issue-date slots only (offer start, offer end, listing day). 0 = mother document and our MCP only
#IPO_HOST_SOURCES=0

# ===== Report fetch =====
# The mother document is submitted once. The script polls that job. It does not send retry.
